    <field name="scopecontent_teim">Window displays: a window in Gimbel&#39;s with small sculpture of a fawn, and men&#39;s shirts; boxes of flowers outside wholesale florists on 6th Avenue; Chinchilla Promotion Agency on Broadway, with neon chinchillas in window; Universal Atomics, advertising transistorized instruments, and with a small sign reading &#34;strike uranium in Catskill Mtns&#34;; Bannerman Fire Arms, military good from Government auction, 501 Broadway; Sam Goody Record shop, 235 W. 49th; Tin Pan Alley Records, advertising stereo tapes and discs; window for &#34;Flowers by Katya&#34; on 8th Avenue; Olevetti typewriter display, showing single typewriter on column set in the sidewalk, Fifth Avenue; the sculpture &#34;Windward&#34; at 200 E. 42nd.</field>
